Origin: EmberBSD.

Linux 6.18 DRM core next to the Linux 5.6 core
==============================================

A kernel has one DRM core: the 5.6 one (attribute drmkms, files in dist/, own
code in drm/) or the 6.18 one (attribute drmkms618, files in dist618/, own code
in drm618/).  Both export the same drm_* symbols with different layouts.  Both
use the same Linux compatibility layer (attributes drmkms_linux, drmkms_i2c;
directories linux/, include/linux, include/asm), so work on the layer serves
both cores.

	dist618/	Linux 6.18.x files, MIT or "GPL-2.0 OR MIT" only, byte for
			byte as upstream (MANIFEST.tsv: sha256, licence class,
			upstream path; LINUX_VERSION)
	drm618/		files.drmkms618, own headers (include/), own rewrites of
			the GPL-only files, gpl-only.tsv, tools/
	prepare-import618.sh	(re)import of dist618, "--verify" checks it

drm618/gpl-only.tsv lists what is not imported and why: GPL-only files, files
without a licence text, uapi headers under "GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note".
The last column names the existing BSD rewrite in drm/ (a Linux 5.6 level one
that has to be brought to 6.18), or "-" when there is none.

Selecting a core
----------------
files.drmkms618 is included from sys/conf/files, but only as a definition of
the attribute drmkms618: no default kernel configuration selects it.  The
tested way to run the 6.18 core is the loadable module sys/modules/drmkms618
(with drmkms618_sched and drmkms618_ttm) in a kernel without the 5.6 core:
configuration GENERIC_ARL_DRM618 (the ARL configuration without the 5.6
drivers).  A kernel with the attribute selected and the core built in has not
been built or tested.
Selecting both cores fails the build on purpose: drm618_exclusive.c is built
for "drmkms618 & drmkms" and contains an #error.  At run time a module of one
core cannot load into a kernel with the other: the module loader refuses
symbols that already exist (kobj_checksyms).  Modules get their own names
(drmkms618, ...) and depend on "drmkms_linux,sysmon_power" like drmkms; a
driver module built for 6.18 depends on "drmkms618" and is not interchangeable
with the 5.6 build of the same driver (the efidrm kernel version guard
already covers that).

Includes the 6.18 sources expect
-------------------------------
dist618 is byte for byte upstream, so what Linux include chains bring in for
it has to come from somewhere else.  Every drmkms618 file is compiled with
-include include/drm618_prefix.h (files.drmkms618; the compile map does the
same, NOPREFIX=1 leaves it out): the includes the sources expect, the renaming
of the NetBSD struct rb_node and of the names both systems define differently
(ALIGN, LIST_HEAD, mutex_init, RB_ROOT, ... see include/drm618_layer.h, chosen
by the number or the type of the arguments).  Headers that exist in the shared
layer with another meaning (linux/wait.h, rbtree.h, kthread.h,
interval_tree_generic.h) are shadowed in include/linux/; the 5.6 core never
sees them.  New names without a clash go into the shared layer.

Local changes to dist618 are made in separate commits after the pristine
import commit, so that "git diff" against the import shows exactly what
EmberBSD changed; BSD-only hooks that can live outside the Linux files go to
drm618/include (it comes first in the include path) or to the layer.
